+## Claims tested, contrary evidence and limits
+
+- *Claim "the Executive is down / neglecting assigned work"* — not supported at review time: a
+  live agent is running and its log shows active work, and the worktree contains in-progress
+  changes. Contrary evidence preserved: nine observations of `executive_unhealthy`, repeated
+  `cycle=false` with running agent, and repeated 300 s / 180 s wrapper timeouts are real and are
+  not erased by the live agent. No Act 9 neglect finding is made: there is no billy-dev
+  assignment at issue in this liveness case, and a health signal is not neglect of a task.
+- *Claim "a clear observation means the cause is repaired and delivery verified"* — not
+  supported: the case is still open with `clear_observations = 0`, the signal re-fired after a
+  single clear sample, and there is no independently verified root-cause repair or new delivery
+  effect. A fresh agent session is not a completed outcome.
+- **Observed measurement limitation (reported, not reformed):** the branch-health probe's own
+  wrapper times out on every sampled invocation yet still emits `executive_unhealthy`, and
+  `readiness` is derived from wrapper exit status plus a transient agent-state probe. The signal
+  therefore measures dispatch/liveness mechanics and can be produced by a probe failure even
+  while the office agent works. The recurrence of `executive_unhealthy` cases that auto-close
+  after 20 clear observations is a repeated liveness pattern, not evidence of useful delivery or
+  its absence. Parliament may consider this; the Judiciary neither proposes nor implements any
+  change to the probe, the collector or the case rules (Act 15 §2).
+- Host note: this is a billy-dev-side operational signal. GitHub-hosted CI is not implicated and
+  no workflow disabling was observed.
+- Limits: no independent host telemetry for the timeout wrapper, no re-run of the Executive
+  suite, and no re-verification of the Act 34 candidate's legal effect. Those are limitations,
